#    465:   4010: ! Execute services routine
#    465:   4011: !
#    465:   4012: ! Executes a services routine by module-local number. All of the input
#    465:   4013: ! parameters are passed on the stack, and the result, if any, also returned on
#    465:   4014: ! the stack.
#    465:   4015: !
#    465:   4016: ! All of the input parameters are removed from the stack, leaving just the
#    465:   4017: ! result (if any).
#    465:   4018: !
#    465:   4019: ! The load of parameters is fairly ad-hoc. Value parameters are simply fetched.
#    465:   4020: ! VAR and VIEW parameters have to be loaded into a buffer to transfer.
#    465:   4021: !
#    465:   4022: ! The layout of the parameters and return are:
#    465:   4023: !
#    465:   4024: ! params+intsize*2: return value
#    465:   4025: ! params+intsize:   param1
#    465:   4026: ! params:           param2
#    465:   4027: ! ...
#    465:   4028: !
#    465:   4029: ! ie., the parameters start at the params address, then climb upwards until the
#    465:   4030: ! return value (if any). The params address should be incremented past all
#    465:   4031: ! parameters, but left pointing at the return value, if any. Otherwise params
#    465:   4032: ! is just left above all parameters.
